::: persist-note
::: dot
✷
:::
**Your basket persists across pages, reloads, and tabs.** Open this page in two tabs, add something in one, and watch the count rise in the other — that's a `:store`, synced over the browser's storage event.
:::

## Built from Markdown

Every product card, the live search, and the running count are written as plain Markdown with a handful of Darkmown directives. The catalog unrolls from a JSON file; the basket is one shared `:store`. No components, no JSX, no hand-written event handlers.

<details class="source-reveal">
<summary>View source — it's Markdown</summary>

```wd
:store cart = []
:computed count = cart.length
:state q = ""

:bind q placeholder="Search the shop…"

::: catalog
@loop /products.json into p where p.name contains q
::: card .product
::: chip
{ p.emoji }
:::
::: body
::: pname
{ p.name }
:::
::: foot
::: price
${ p.price }
:::
:button "Add" -> cart += p
:::
:::
:::
@empty
Nothing matches "{ q }".
@endloop
:::
```

</details>

